@startuml session-start-today
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Starting a hosted primary session today (task-board claude)

actor "Person" as P $PERSON
participant "task-board claude\n(wrapper)" as W $SERVICE
participant "tb-sessiond\n(one control plane per board)" as D $SERVICE
participant "Claude provider host\n(PTY master held by tb-sessiond)" as H $SERVICE
participant "Claude Code" as C $AGENT
database "Board\n(board-goal-v2)" as B $COMMITTED

P -> W: task-board claude
W -> W: validate the launch plan,\nrun primary-session preparation
W -> D: ConnectOrStart(board key)
D -> D: is the parent/primary slot free?\n(one primary session per board)
D -> H: Launch(provider launch request)
H -> C: start in a PTY
D -> B: read the parent/primary head
D -> H: ApplyBoardGoal(revision)
H -> C: /goal tbg-<token> [board goal <ID> rev <N> ...] <condition>
C --> H: rendered acknowledgement of that revision
H --> D: applied_goal_ref = head
D --> W: attachment
W <-> C: terminal, relayed through the daemon
...
P -> W: detach
W --> P: anthropic-board resume SES-...
note over C
  keeps running without a client;
  the native goal evaluator
  drives continuation
end note

caption Sources: skill-project-management docs/claude-goal-runtime.md; internal/sessionmanager/host.go, claude_host.go, key.go
@enduml
